                <section class="s_text_block o_colored_level pt32 pb32">
                    <p>Ready to give reclaimed wood or old furniture a new life? This workshop is for makers who already know their way around basic hand and power tools and want to take their creativity—and sustainability—to the next level. Bring in a small wooden piece, scrap timber, or a project you’re ready to refresh or reinvent, and we’ll guide you through the process of transforming it into something beautiful and functional.</p>
                    <p>We’ll cover techniques like sanding, joinery repairs, custom cutting, surface finishing, and adding new features like handles, legs, or shelving. This is a great opportunity to experiment with design, get advice on grain and structural stability, and work in a creative community of fellow woodworkers.</p>
                    <p>The goal is not perfection—it’s expression, exploration, and extending the life of your timber. Whether you're turning an old pallet into a plant stand, a drawer into a floating shelf, or simply restoring a worn-out side table, you’ll leave with a reimagined wooden piece you can actually.</p>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Please Bring:</strong>
                    </p>
